{%- comment -%}
  APEX hero.

  Sits under the overlay header, so it owns the full viewport from y=0 and the
  header floats on top of it. Content is vertically CENTRED in a right-hand
  column on desktop, and BOTTOM-anchored full-width on mobile — that difference
  is measured from the two mockups, not a convenience.

  The wordmark is the same lockup the header uses, so it can never drift from
  the header logo. It is wrapped in the page <h1> with a visually-hidden text
  equivalent — an SVG alone gives the page no heading.

  BACKGROUND VIDEO. `Background` switches the media between the image and a
  video; the video crops to fill on exactly the same rules, sharing the
  breakpoint focal points rather than inventing its own. It is muted, looping
  and inert — no controls, no picture-in-picture, out of the tab order and
  hidden from assistive tech, because it carries no information the copy does
  not already carry.

  It never renders alone. Whatever the video is, a poster frame paints first
  (its own preview, or the image below it), so the hero is composed before a
  single video byte lands and stays composed if the browser refuses to
  autoplay — low-power mode and a data saver both do.

  The pause control is not decoration. WCAG 2.2.2 wants a way to stop any
  motion that starts on its own and runs past five seconds, and a looping hero
  is exactly that. `prefers-reduced-motion` starts it paused on the poster
  instead, and the button follows the video's own play/pause events rather
  than tracking state of its own, so a browser-blocked autoplay still shows
  the honest label.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign img = section.settings.image
  assign has_picked_image = false
  if img != blank
    assign has_picked_image = true
  endif

  # Resolved separately: filters cannot be chained inside an image_tag
  # argument — `alt: img.alt | default: x` would apply default to the whole
  # rendered tag, not to the alt value.
  #
  # The heading is no longer usable as a fallback: it is now a multi-line
  # statement, not the brand name, and it would read as a caption for a
  # photograph it does not describe.
  assign hero_alt = img.alt | default: shop.name

  assign vid = section.settings.video
  assign use_video = false
  if section.settings.background_type == 'video' and vid != blank
    assign use_video = true
  endif

  comment
    Poster. The video's own preview frame first — it is a frame OF the video,
    so the swap from poster to playback is invisible. The picked image is the
    next best thing, and the named file is the last resort, mirroring the
    image branch below.
  endcomment
  if use_video
    if vid.preview_image != blank
      assign poster_url = vid.preview_image | image_url: width: 2000
    elsif has_picked_image
      assign poster_url = img | image_url: width: 2000
    else
      assign poster_url = section.settings.fallback_image_name | file_url
    endif
  endif
-%}

<section
  class="hero"
  style="
    --hero-min-h: calc(100svh - 170px);
    --hero-overlay: {{ section.settings.overlay_opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};
    --hero-logo-w-mobile: {{ section.settings.logo_width_mobile }}px;
    --hero-logo-w-desktop: {{ section.settings.logo_width_desktop }}px;
    --hero-focus-x-mobile: {{ section.settings.focus_x_mobile }}%;
    --hero-focus-x-desktop: {{ section.settings.focus_x_desktop }}%;
  "
>
  <div class="hero__media">
    {%- if use_video -%}
      <video
        class="hero__video"
        data-hero-video
        autoplay
        muted
        loop
        playsinline
        preload="auto"
        disablepictureinpicture
        tabindex="-1"
        aria-hidden="true"
        {% if poster_url != blank %}
          poster="{{ poster_url }}"
        {% endif %}
      >
        {%- comment -%}
          Shopify's own transcodes, in the order it hands them over: HLS where
          a browser speaks it, progressive MP4 everywhere else. This is why the
          picker is worth using over a raw file URL — a .mov straight out of
          Content > Files is video/quicktime, which Chrome and Firefox will
          not play.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- for source in vid.sources -%}
          <source src="{{ source.url }}" type="{{ source.mime_type }}">
        {%- endfor -%}
      </video>
    {%- elsif has_picked_image -%}
      {{
        img
        | image_url: width: 3000
        | image_tag:
          loading: 'eager',
          fetchpriority: 'high',
          sizes: '100vw',
          widths: '600, 900, 1200, 1600, 2000, 2600, 3000',
          class: 'hero__image',
          alt: hero_alt
      }}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Fallback to a file uploaded under Content > Files, so the section renders
        before anyone opens the Theme Editor. Picking an image in the editor is
        preferable — it gives responsive srcset and a focal point.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <img
        class="hero__image"
        src="{{ section.settings.fallback_image_name | file_url }}"
        alt="{{ shop.name | escape }}"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      >
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="apex-container hero__inner">
    <div class="hero__content">
      {%- comment -%}
        The lockup is aria-hidden: it is a picture of the brand name, and the
        header already announces it. The <h1> below carries real text now, so
        hiding it costs the document outline nothing — which is what closes
        the "mobile homepage has no <h1>" concern in CLAUDE.md.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.show_lockup -%}
        <span class="hero__lockup" aria-hidden="true">
          {% render 'svg-icons', icon: 'apex-lockup-stacked' %}
        </span>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
        <h1 class="hero__heading">
          {{- section.settings.heading | escape | newline_to_br -}}
        </h1>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="hero__heading">ENGINEERED PERFECTION<span style="font-size: 0.5em; position: relative; top: -0.7em;">™</span></p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.supporting_line != blank -%}
        <p class="hero__supporting">{{ section.settings.supporting_line | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
        <a
          class="btn btn-light hero__cta"
          {% if section.settings.cta_link != blank %}
            href="{{ section.settings.cta_link }}"
          {% else %}
            href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}"
          {% endif %}
        >
          {{ section.settings.cta_label | escape }}
          {%- if section.settings.cta_show_arrow -%}
            {% render 'icon-arrow-right' %}
          {%- endif -%}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if use_video -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Outside .hero__media on purpose: that layer sits at z-index -1 so the
      photograph can pass behind the copy, and nothing inside it can be
      clicked.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <apex-hero-video>
      <button
        class="hero__video-toggle"
        type="button"
        aria-pressed="false"
        aria-label="{{ 'sections.video.pause_video' | t }}"
        data-label-play="{{ 'sections.video.play_video' | t | escape }}"
        data-label-pause="{{ 'sections.video.pause_video' | t | escape }}"
      >
        <span class="hero__video-icon hero__video-icon--pause">
          {% render 'svg-icons', icon: 'pause' %}
        </span>
        <span class="hero__video-icon hero__video-icon--play">
          {% render 'svg-icons', icon: 'play' %}
        </span>
      </button>
    </apex-hero-video>

    <script>
      if (!customElements.get('apex-hero-video')) {
        customElements.define(
          'apex-hero-video',
          class ApexHeroVideo extends HTMLElement {
            connectedCallback() {
              this.video = this.closest('.hero')?.querySelector('[data-hero-video]');
              this.button = this.querySelector('button');
              if (!this.video || !this.button) return;

              // The button reports the VIDEO's state rather than the state it
              // thinks it set. Autoplay is a request, not a guarantee — Safari
              // in low-power mode and every data saver refuse it — and reading
              // back from the element is what keeps the label honest when they
              // do.
              this.sync = () => {
                const paused = this.video.paused;
                this.button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', paused ? 'true' : 'false');
                this.button.setAttribute(
                  'aria-label',
                  paused ? this.button.dataset.labelPlay : this.button.dataset.labelPause
                );
              };

              this.video.addEventListener('play', this.sync);
              this.video.addEventListener('pause', this.sync);

              this.button.addEventListener('click', () => {
                if (this.video.paused) {
                  this.video.play().catch(this.sync);
                } else {
                  this.video.pause();
                }
              });

              this.motionQuery = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
              this.applyMotion = () => {
                if (this.motionQuery.matches) {
                  this.video.pause();
                } else if (this.video.autoplay) {
                  this.video.play().catch(this.sync);
                }
              };
              this.motionQuery.addEventListener('change', this.applyMotion);

              this.applyMotion();
              this.sync();
            }

            disconnectedCallback() {
              this.video?.removeEventListener('play', this.sync);
              this.video?.removeEventListener('pause', this.sync);
              this.motionQuery?.removeEventListener('change', this.applyMotion);
            }
          }
        );
      }
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    min-height: var(--hero-min-h, 100svh);
    isolation: isolate;
    text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
  }
  .hero svg {
      filter: drop-shadow(2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5));
  }
  .hero .btn {
    text-shadow: none;
  }

  .hero__media {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .hero__image,
  .hero__video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    /* Horizontal focus is per-breakpoint because `cover` crops a different
       axis at each shape. The supplied photograph is ~4:3 with the subject in
       the left 45%: a desktop viewport is WIDER than 4:3, so nothing is
       cropped horizontally and this value is inert there. A phone is far
       taller, leaving only ~35% of the source width visible — and `left` would
       window onto 0-35%, cutting the ball and hand out of frame completely.
       Mobile therefore pulls toward the subject; desktop pins it left so it
       stays clear of the right-hand copy column. Vertical stays centred: the
       composition has headroom top and bottom and needs no tuning. */
    object-position: var(--hero-focus-x-mobile, 40%) center;
  }
  .hero__video {
    filter: grayscale(100%) contrast(1.3) brightness(0.8);
  }

  /* Optional scrim. Defaults to 0 because the supplied photograph already
     falls off to near-black where the copy sits — raise it only if a
     replacement image leaves the text short of contrast. */
  .hero__media::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
    opacity: var(--hero-overlay, 0);
  }

  .hero__inner {
    display: flex;
    /* Mobile: content sits at the bottom of the frame, over the darker
       lower third of the photograph. Measured, not assumed. */
    align-items: flex-end;
    padding-block: calc(var(--header-height) + var(--space-md)) var(--space-lg);
  }

  .hero__content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    /* Right-aligned at BOTH breakpoints — the copy block hangs off the right
       edge of the container and the ragged edge runs down its right side. */
    align-items: flex-end;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    width: 100%;
    text-align: end;
  }

  /* --- lockup ----------------------------------------------------------
     Decorative and aria-hidden (see the markup). Sized by the two schema
     controls, which is why it keeps the horizontal lockup's width tokens
     rather than the banner's fixed 219px. */

  .hero__lockup {
    display: block;
    width: var(--hero-logo-w-mobile, 18.4rem);
    max-width: 100%;
    line-height: 0;
  }

  .hero__lockup svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* --- eyebrow ----------------------------------------------------------
     This section's own original eyebrow treatment, restored: hero scale
     (--text-lead), not the --text-xs used by the band eyebrows further down
     the page. Bronze italic, per the "italic is a role" rule in CLAUDE.md.

     No margin — .hero__content is a flex column with gap: var(--space-sm),
     which already sets it off the heading below. */
  .hero__eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--brand-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-eyebrow);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* --- heading ----------------------------------------------------------
     Set exactly as .athlete-banner__heading is — same family, weight,
     tracking, leading, colour and case — so the two bands read as one
     system. Only the size differs: the banner steps down on mobile to clear
     the portrait beside it, and the hero has nothing beside it, so it rides
     the shared ramp instead of carrying a one-off. */
  .hero__heading {
    max-width: 35rem; /* 350px — the banner's mobile measure */
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--text-h3);
    font-weight: var(--weight-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-display);
    line-height: var(--leading-heading);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* --- supporting line -------------------------------------------------- */

  .hero__supporting {
    max-width: 34ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-h4);
    line-height: var(--leading-body);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* The mockup sets the CTA further from the copy than the other gaps. */
  .hero__cta {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-xs);
  }

  /* --- video pause control ---------------------------------------------

     Bottom LEFT. It was bottom right, opposite copy that used to be
     left-aligned on mobile; now the copy is right-aligned at both
     breakpoints and bottom-anchored on mobile, so the right corner is
     exactly where the CTA lands. Square, because --radius-* is 0 across
     this theme. */

  apex-hero-video {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-end: var(--space-md);
    inset-inline-start: var(--gutter);
    z-index: 1;
    display: block;
  }

  .hero__video-toggle {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 4rem;
    height: 4rem;
    padding: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-bg) 55%, transparent);
    color: var(--color-text);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-out),
      border-color var(--motion-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .hero__video-toggle:hover {
      border-color: var(--color-text);
      background-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-bg) 80%, transparent);
    }
  }

  .hero__video-toggle:focus-visible {
    outline: var(--focus-ring-width) solid var(--color-focus);
    outline-offset: var(--focus-ring-offset);
  }

  /* Both icons occupy the same cell, so the button never changes size as the
     glyph swaps. aria-pressed is the single source of truth for which shows -
     the state lives in the attribute the screen reader reads, not beside it. */
  .hero__video-icon {
    grid-area: 1 / 1;
    display: none;
    line-height: 0;
  }

  .hero__video-icon svg {
    display: block;
    width: 1.6rem;
    height: 1.6rem;
  }

  .hero__video-toggle[aria-pressed='false'] .hero__video-icon--pause,
  .hero__video-toggle[aria-pressed='true'] .hero__video-icon--play {
    display: block;
  }

  /* --- desktop --------------------------------------------------------- */

  @media screen and (min-width: 990px) {
    .hero__image,
    .hero__video {
      object-position: var(--hero-focus-x-desktop, 0%) center;
    }

    .hero__inner {
      /* Vertically centred rather than bottom-anchored. */
      align-items: center;
      padding-block: var(--header-height);
    }

    .hero__content {
      /* Right-hand column. The mockup places this at ~58% across the
         container; a col-start-8 grid span lands within ~30px and keeps the
         hero on the same 12-column rhythm as every other band. */
      gap: var(--space-sm);
      width: auto;
      max-width: 52rem;
      margin-inline-start: auto;
    }

    .hero__lockup {
      width: var(--hero-logo-w-desktop, 24rem);
    }

    .hero__heading {
      max-width: 46rem; /* 460px — the banner's desktop measure */
      font-size: var(--text-h2);
    }

    .hero__cta {
      margin-block-start: var(--space-xs);
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "APEX hero",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "apex-hero-section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Background"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "background_type",
      "label": "Background",
      "options": [
        { "value": "image", "label": "Image" },
        { "value": "video", "label": "Video" }
      ],
      "default": "image"
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video",
      "label": "Background video",
      "info": "Silent, looping, and cropped to fill exactly as the image is. Pick it here rather than pasting a file URL — Shopify serves its own MP4 and HLS transcodes, so a .mov uploaded to Content > Files plays in every browser. The image below is still used as the poster frame."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Background image",
      "info": "Recommended: 2600px wide or more. Falls back to the file named below if empty."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "fallback_image_name",
      "label": "Fallback file name",
      "info": "A file uploaded under Content > Files. Used only when no image is picked above.",
      "default": "apex-background-2.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "focus_x_mobile",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "label": "Horizontal focus, mobile",
      "info": "A phone crops the sides hard — only about a third of the image width is visible. 40% keeps the ball and hand in frame; 0% would show only the left edge.",
      "default": 40
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "focus_x_desktop",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "label": "Horizontal focus, desktop",
      "info": "Pins the subject left, clear of the copy column. Has no visible effect once the viewport is wider than the image's own ratio, since nothing is cropped horizontally there.",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "overlay_opacity",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 80,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "label": "Darken image",
      "info": "Leave at 0 for the supplied photograph — it is already dark where the copy sits.",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "height",
      "min": 60,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "%",
      "label": "Height, share of viewport",
      "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Content"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_lockup",
      "label": "Show APEX lockup",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "info": "Bronze italic callout above the heading. Set in uppercase automatically.",
      "default": "Engineered perfection."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "info": "The page's H1. Each line break is kept as a line break. Set in uppercase automatically.",
      "default": "The ball\nserious players\nchoose."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "supporting_line",
      "label": "Supporting line",
      "default": "Trusted from local courts to championship weekends."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Call to action"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_label",
      "label": "Button label",
      "default": "Shop Apex 48"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "cta_link",
      "label": "Button link"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "cta_show_arrow",
      "label": "Show arrow on button",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Lockup size"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "logo_width_mobile",
      "min": 120,
      "max": 320,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Wordmark width, mobile",
      "default": 184
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "logo_width_desktop",
      "min": 160,
      "max": 480,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Wordmark width, desktop",
      "default": 240
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "APEX hero"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
